---
import BioDemo from "../layouts/BioDemo.astro";
---

<BioDemo
	title="biomorphic ui — spikes"
	material="spikes"
	toggleStates="active,wall"
	toggleLabels="grow spikes|clear spikes"
>
	<h1>spikes</h1>
	<p class="lead">
		A reach-field CA grown onto frozen substrate cells. Each box is its
		own group; neighbours block but never seed each other.
	</p>

	<section class="card sub" data-bio-group="card">
		<h2>Substrate card</h2>
		<p>
			This box is a region of immutable cells. The spikes take root on its
			perimeter and grow outward, stopping at the next box.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="card sub tall" data-bio-group="crevice">
		<h2>Crevice partner</h2>
		<p>
			The gap between these two boxes is a constrained channel — spikes
			from both sides meet in the middle.
		</p>
	</section>

	<div class="shapes">
		<div class="sub shape circle" data-bio-group="shapes" data-shape="circle">
			<span>circle</span>
		</div>
		<div
			class="sub shape star"
			data-bio-group="shapes"
			data-shape="star"
			data-points="5"
		>
			<span>star</span>
		</div>
		<div
			class="sub shape hex"
			data-bio-group="shapes"
			data-shape="polygon"
			data-sides="6"
		>
			<span>hexagon</span>
		</div>
	</div>

	<section class="card sub faq" data-bio-group="faq">
		<h2>Self-resizing group</h2>
		<p>
			One group whose <em>own</em> rect changes. Opening a row below grows
			this box, so the runtime re-rasterizes and re-grows the spikes around
			the new perimeter — the faq counter ticks. Neighbours below only
			translate.
		</p>
		<details>
			<summary>Why does a resize rebuild?</summary>
			<p>
				The substrate grid was rasterized at the old height; every cell
				must keep its coordinate, so the field is invalid until it is
				rebuilt. Growth is deterministic, so the regrow is faithful.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>Why doesn't a resize just translate?</summary>
			<p>
				A pure translation keeps every cell aligned, so a frozen frame can
				slide as one piece. A height change moves the perimeter relative to
				the cells, so the seed band itself changes.
			</p>
		</details>
	</section>

	<details
		class="reflow"
		data-bio-regrow-on="close"
		data-bio-regrow-group="toggle"
		data-bio-regrow-gate="regrowOnClose"
	>
		<summary>group-relative reflow</summary>
		<div class="reflow-body">
			<p>
				Every box here is its own group. Opening this panel grows the gap
				and slides the toggle below down as one piece. Once a group has
				settled, moving it just <em>translates</em> the finished shape — a
				jigsaw piece — instead of re-growing it. Closing this panel moves
				the toggle back toward the shapes above; with <em>regrow on
				close</em> ticked the toggle is rebuilt so its spikes re-fit the
				new layout instead of sliding over the group above (its counter
				then ticks).
			</p>
			<label class="check">
				<span>regrow toggle on close</span>
				<input id="regrowOnClose" type="checkbox" checked />
			</label>
			<div class="status">
				re-seeds — shapes: <b data-reseed="shapes">0</b> · toggle:
				<b data-reseed="toggle">0</b> · faq: <b data-reseed="faq">0</b>
			</div>
		</div>
	</details>

	<div class="row">
		<button
			class="btn sub"
			id="growthBtn"
			data-bio-group="toggle"
			data-bio-mode="active"
		>
			grow spikes
		</button>
	</div>
</BioDemo>
